  "equipment_type": "Power meter via BACnet gateway",
  "applies_to": "BEST Eniscope power meters whose data is pushed (MQTT) to a Chipkin CAS-2700-74 BEST Gateway.",
  "summary": "The Chipkin BEST Gateway receives Eniscope meter data over MQTT and serves it on BACnet IP. Objects are created automatically as data arrives, named with the Eniscope channel codes (P, Q, S, E, V, I, PF and so on, with 1-3 for the phase). This list is the one-meter sample printed in the manual: 57 Analog Inputs plus a time stamp.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "From table 5-1, \"Sample BACnet Object List\" (one meter). The object list is dynamic: objects are mapped in the order data arrives, so instance numbers can differ on a real gateway. Check the gateway report page for the real list.",
    "Names are Eniscope channel codes, kept as printed; the manual does not define them. Units are as printed with the sample.",
    "PIV 16 \"ts\" is a time stamp in seconds (Unix time in the sample value).",
    "There is no access column; all objects are read-only."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Chipkin BEST Gateway User Manual (CAS-2700-74)",
    "doc_number": "CAS-2700-74",
    "revision_date": "Rev 3, 2018-06-11",
    "url": "https://cdn.chipkin.com/assets/uploads/2019/Jun/CAS_MAN_CAS-2700-74_BEST-Gateway_Manual_26-15-12-54.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the BACnet port, device instance and device name on the BEST Config page, let the Eniscope system publish to the gateway, then discover the objects and map them by name from the report page.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 48",
        "name": "P",
        "why": "Total active power, W"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 9",
        "name": "E",
        "why": "Energy total, Wh"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 40",
        "name": "Q",
        "why": "Total reactive power, VAR"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "PF",
        "why": "Power factor"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 38",
        "name": "V",
        "why": "Voltage, V"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 25",
        "name": "I",
        "why": "Current, A"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 29",
        "name": "F",
        "why": "Frequency, Hz"
      },
      {
        "ref": "PIV 16",
        "name": "ts",
        "why": "Time stamp of the data, s"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": "If the gateway loses its data source or a value cannot be read, the object Out_Of_Service is set true and the last good value stays in Present_Value.",
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "BACnet IP on UDP 47808 by default; set the device instance and name on the BEST Config page and reboot after changing the port.",
      "Eniscope data arrives over MQTT on TCP 1883 (configurable).",
      "Discovery across subnets needs a BBMD supplied by the BAS installer."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Map objects by name, not by instance: instances follow the order the gateway first received each value.",
      "Watch Out_Of_Service to spot stale data."
    ]
  },
